      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Listen, you're dealing with a concussion, and that's no joke. But let's get real—taking double doses of magnesium isn't going to clear the fog any faster, and mixing it with Aleve isn't a good idea. Aleve can mess with your stomach and might even make your dizziness worse. Stick to the recommended doses of B12 and magnesium. If the fog's still there after an hour, it's not a sign to up the dose. Your brain needs time to recover, and pushing it too hard could do more harm than good. And don't even think about working if you're still spinning like a top. Rest is your best friend right now. When you can, get that doc's appointment. But until then, keep it simple and safe. Your brain's healing, so give it the time it needs.",
